# Absences

This feature allows you to manage your members' absences and automatically deduct absent <%= Basket.model_name.human(count: 2).downcase %> from your deliveries. Your members can announce their absences directly from their member area. You can also add absences for your members as an admin ([Other > Absences](/absences)).

## Configuration {#configuration}

Once this additional feature is activated in [your settings](/settings), [multiple settings](/settings#absence) are available.

The **notice period** is counted until midnight, X days before the delivery date. Example: 3 days before a Wednesday delivery means Sunday midnight. After that, members cannot announce the absence from their account. Admins still can from [Absences](/absences).

A member says they announced an absence and it does not show? Check the deadline, the membership year, and whether the email was only a message, not a saved absence.

### Canceling {#canceling}

Canceling restores the original delivery. Shifting moves the <%= Basket.model_name.human.downcase %> to another date.

- **Admins**: cancel from [Absences](/absences), not from the basket row on the membership. The basket row "move" is a [shift](#basket-shift).
- **Members**: cancel from their account while the notice period is still open.

## Billing {#billing}

By default, <%= Basket.model_name.human(count: 2).downcase %> marked as absent and not delivered are billed, and members are advised to find an acquaintance to collect their <%= Basket.model_name.human.downcase %> in their place. In [the settings](/settings#absence), you can also choose not to bill them. The system will then automatically [adjust the billing](/handbook/billing#price-change) of the membership.

If a member is away but still wants to pay, do not mark an absence, or keep billing absences in the settings. Marking them absent is what creates a credit when billing is off.

## <%= Basket.model_name.human %> Shifts {#basket-shift}

It is possible to shift the delivery of a <%= Basket.model_name.human.downcase %> during an absence to another delivery. This allows members to compensate for their absences without changing the number of <%= Basket.model_name.human(count: 2).downcase %> billed.

On the admin side, simply modify a <%= Basket.model_name.human.downcase %> marked as absent from the membership page and choose another delivery date. The <%= Basket.model_name.human.downcase %> content (including complements) will then be automatically shifted to the chosen <%= Basket.model_name.human.downcase %>.

On the member side, <%= Basket.model_name.human.downcase %> shifting is not possible by default. To activate this feature, you have the option to [modify the following settings](/settings#absence):

- **Number of allowed shifts**: to limit, if you wish, the number of shifts possible by members.
- **Deadline for shifts**: to limit, if you wish, the shifts possible in time.

If the absence is canceled, the <%= Basket.model_name.human.downcase %> content is automatically restored to its original delivery.

> An included absence can also be shifted. Its <%= Basket.model_name.human.downcase %> content is then billed on the target delivery and the absence does not count toward the membership's included absences. The unused included absence remains available and, when possible, is provisionally assigned to another delivery.

### Newsletter Template

When a <%= Basket.model_name.human.downcase %> has received shifts, you can display a reminder in your [newsletter templates](/newsletter_templates) using the `basket.shifted` and `basket.shifts` variables:

~~~ liquid
{% if basket and basket.shifted %}
  {% highlight %}
    <p><strong>📣 Important reminder!</strong></p>
    <p>You have <strong>{{ basket.quantity }} <%= Basket.model_name.human(count: 2).downcase %></strong> to pick up this week:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your regular <%= Basket.model_name.human.downcase %></li>
      {% for shift in basket.shifts %}
        <li><%= Basket.model_name.human %> shifted from {{ shift.old_delivery_date }}</li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  {% endhighlight %}
{% endif %}
~~~

## Included Absences {#absence-included}

It is possible to configure a number of absences included in the membership. These absences are then automatically deducted and not billed from the start of the membership. The system will provisionally mark the last deliveries of the membership as absent, while waiting for the member to fix these absences on specific dates. Additional absences will be billed or not according to the mode chosen in [your settings](/settings#absence).

> Set the number of included absences on each [delivery cycle](/handbook/deliveries#delivery-cycles) so that [your registration form](<%= new_members_member_url(subdomain: Current.org.members_subdomain) %>) can offer memberships with the corresponding number of deliveries.

### Calculation of included absences {#absence-included-logic}

The cycle number is for a full fiscal year. By default, the membership quota is calculated in proportion to the number of <%= Basket.model_name.human(count: 2).downcase %>.

This can be changed with [Liquid syntax](https://shopify.github.io/liquid) in [the settings](/settings#absence).

Default:

~~~ liquid
{{ membership.baskets | divided_by: membership.full_year_deliveries | times: membership.full_year_absences_included | round }}
~~~

Available variables:

- **membership.baskets**: <%= Basket.model_name.human(count: 2) %> of the membership
- **membership.full_year_deliveries**: deliveries in a full year for this cycle
- **membership.full_year_absences_included**: full-year included absences (cycle default or membership override)
- **membership.started_fy_month**: month of the start date in the fiscal year (1-12, 1 is the first month of the configured fiscal year)
- **membership.started_day**: calendar day of the start date (1-31)
- **membership.basket_size_id** / **membership.depot_id** / **membership.depot_group_id** / **membership.delivery_cycle_id**: related IDs

`started_fy_month` follows the organization's fiscal year. For a May fiscal year, May is 1 and August is 4.

Example: no included absences after the 13th of the fourth fiscal month (April when the year starts in January, August when it starts in May):

~~~ liquid
{% if membership.started_fy_month > 4 or membership.started_fy_month == 4 and membership.started_day >= 13 %}
  0
{% else %}
  {{ membership.baskets | divided_by: membership.full_year_deliveries | times: membership.full_year_absences_included | round }}
{% endif %}
~~~

Changing the logic does not rewrite existing memberships until each one is updated, or until a delivery or cycle update resyncs them. That can change billed <%= Basket.model_name.human(count: 2).downcase %>. The included-absences reminder timestamp is not reset.

### End-of-Year Mode {#absence-included-mode}

When members don't use all their included absences by the end of their membership, the remaining absences stay provisionally marked on the last deliveries. To handle this situation, you can configure an **end-of-year mode** in [the settings](/settings#absence):

**Provisional Absence Respected**

This is the default mode. Provisional absences will not be delivered. Members will receive a reminder email and can then choose to force a delivery from their account if they want to receive <%= Basket.model_name.human(count: 2).downcase %> that were marked as provisionally absent.

This mode is useful when you prefer that unused absences remain as absences by default, giving members the option to request delivery if needed.

**Delivery of Remaining Absences**

In this mode, unused included absences will have their delivery forced and billed at reminder time. Members receive a reminder email and can report an absence to opt out before the delivery happens and is billed.

This mode is useful when you prefer that members receive their <%= Basket.model_name.human(count: 2).downcase %> by default, avoiding the confusion of members showing up expecting a <%= Basket.model_name.human.downcase %> that wasn't prepared.

### Reminder Email {#absence-included-reminder}

A reminder email is sent to members with unused included absences a configurable number of weeks before the first provisional absence (default: 4 weeks). This gives members time to take action according to the chosen mode:

- **In "Provisional Absence Respected" mode**: Force a delivery if they want to receive <%= Basket.model_name.human(count: 2).downcase %> that were marked as provisionally absent.
- **In "Delivery of Remaining Absences" mode**: Report an absence to opt out of deliveries they don't want.
